--- ocompiler-2.orig/localtest
+++ ocompiler-2/localtest
@@ -1 +1 @@
-2-5+239
+2-5+240
--- ocompiler-2.orig/o.html
+++ ocompiler-2/o.html
@@ -788,7 +788,7 @@ format elfobj64<br>
         #A Hello World program<br>
         #the default format is Format Exe<br>
         Library "user32.dll"<br>
-        Import "MessageBoxA" Message 4 #extra 4 can be used by otoc<br>
+        Import "MessageBoxA" Message 4v #4v is used by otoc, 4 arguments, and V/v varargs if present<br>
         Char program="Program"<br>
         vStr title^program<br>
         Char data="Hello World"<br>
@@ -981,10 +981,14 @@ format elfobj64<br>
 <p>There are at least two options at the '*' wildcard from there. '{}' is an enumeration.</p>
 <p>First long(4 bytes) is null or offset of entry which will be at the end.</p>
 <p>Xfile_noignore at ocompiler is '^' sign before the command, and at otoc will noignore a tagIgnore argument. Xfile_yesignore at compiler is '!' sign before the command and at otoc will ignore the command.</p>
+<p>Another option specific to otoc is Xfile_declvolatile_yes, to use stack variables at o for recursion but not pointers at c (example: sdu ?attr).</p>
